cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this method, please cite it as below."
title: "constraint-compliance: a use-time gate that compiles a taught rule into an auditable goal"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chi"
    given-names: "Guangyao"
    alias: "B1lli"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/B1lli/constraint-compliance"
abstract: >
  An agent skill for long-running, multi-turn assistants. When a request falls under a rule the
  user taught earlier (persisted in a project instruction file, a memory note, or a learned item),
  the agent itself decides at use time whether the delivery is worth a hard-compliance gate,
  writes an intent statement, picks a level (L2/L3/L4), compiles the rule into a rubric of
  verifiable criteria, sets a goal, audits the deliverable against the rubric before declaring
  completion, and responds to an independent advisory evaluator. Rubric and goal are generated
  from the taught rule at use time rather than hand-written in advance.
keywords:
  - agent skills
  - instruction following
  - self-evolving agents
  - learned constraints
  - acceptance criteria
  - goal loop
